    "summary": "Man&#039;s gown (tobe, boubou, riga). The body is composed of 142 uniform narrow strips of white cotton, hand-spun and hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The strips forming the body of the gown have been sewn vertically, while the sleeves are sewn horizontally. At the front is sewn a large pocket. The pocket, and back and front of the shoulder are hand-embroidered in a darker thread of wild silk with the &#039;two knives&#039; pattern in satin stitch and button-hole eyelet stitch. The sleeves are hemmed, while the neck and bottom of the garment are not.",
